# REGRESSION -- Track B3 (D31-uniform, indirect call sigil gate): the MIRROR of
# `indirect_call_bare_arg_amp_callee_error.gg`. An `&`-spelled argument passed
# into a `Callable[void(int)]` LOCAL whose parameter declares BARE (borrow, no
# sigil) must REJECT at `gg check` with `E_OwnershipMismatch`. Under D31 the
# sigil is CONTRACTUAL at every call site: a caller cannot ADD `&` where the
# callee did not declare it (the callee gets a by-value copy, so the caller's
# `&` intent would be silently discarded).
#
# AXIS / CELL:
#   Callable LOCAL callee  x  `&` arg vs bare-declared param (mirror of E2)
#
# Pre-B3 (RED-verified at HEAD 1028972f): `gg check` printed "OK: no semantic
# errors" and the emitted binary silently dropped the `&` -- the caller's local
# was NOT mutated even though the syntactic intent said "write-through".
# Post-B3: `gg check` REJECTS with `E_OwnershipMismatch`; the silent-drop is
# unreachable by construction.
void bare(int n):
    n = n + 100

void main():
    int a = 1
    Callable[void(int)] cb = bare
    # THE ASSERTION: `cb(&a)` REJECTS -- callee is bare-declared, caller
    # cannot ADD a sigil the callee did not contract for. Correct spelling is
    # bare `cb(a)` (the callee's mutation stays local to its own copy).
    cb(&a)
    print(a)
